      "data": {
        "label": "EXAMPLE — C4 Component: Legacy Sync Service\n\nIllustrates: the third and final level of the C4 drill-down (Context → Container → Component) — deliberately the thinnest of the seven component diagrams. This service is transitional (see its own Container-level details), so it isn't built with the same layered structure as the services meant to last — two components, not three or four.\nPersona: the same technical/solution architect on the modernization task force.\n\nColor key: blue = internal components. Grey = the external system. All edges are dashed, same transitional convention as the Context and Container diagrams.\n\nPart of the Meridian Rail example gallery — epic 0022 (docs/planning/epics/0022-example-diagram-gallery.md)."
      }
    },
